## Permitted Purpose

"**Permitted Purpose**" means any Noncommercial Purpose, as defined
below. A use is a "**Commercial Purpose**" — and is **not** a
Permitted Purpose, and is **not licensed under these terms** —
if it is primarily intended for or directed toward commercial
advantage or monetary compensation. Without limiting that standard,
each of the following is always a Commercial Purpose:

(a) selling the Software, or any part of it, or any product or
service that includes it, for money or other compensation;

(b) requiring payment, a paid subscription, a "tip," a "donation,"
or any other form of compensation as a condition of accessing,
downloading, or using the Software or any copy of it;

(c) generating advertising revenue from any page, app, or service
whose primary purpose is distributing the Software, including
ad-gated download links, forced redirects, or link shorteners used
for ad revenue;

(d) bundling the Software into any paid product, paid modpack, or
monetized server offering; or

(e) any other use primarily intended for or directed toward
commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

### Noncommercial Purposes

Personal use for research, learning, experimentation, testing,
private entertainment, hobby projects, amateur pursuits, or
religious observance, without any anticipated Commercial Purpose,
is a Permitted Purpose. This includes modifying the Software and
publicly sharing your modified version at no cost, provided no part
of that distribution is a Commercial Purpose under (a)–(e) above.

Use by a charitable organization, educational institution, public
research organization, public safety or health organization,
environmental protection organization, or government institution is
a Permitted Purpose regardless of the source of funding, unless that
specific use independently qualifies as a Commercial Purpose under
(a)–(e) above.

If you are unsure whether your intended use is a Commercial Purpose,
contact the Licensor before proceeding — see the Contact section of
[COPYRIGHT.md](./COPYRIGHT.md).

